You are an expert full-stack developer specialized in creating professional desktop tools for visual novel modding. Your task is to design and build a complete, polished, modern desktop application called "LucyEditor" specifically for modding the game Lucy -The Eternity She Wished For-.
Core Goal
Create a comfortable, feature-rich editor that allows community to easily edit the game’s scripts (.txt files inside Scripts.nkpack), add new content, preview changes, and repack everything with one click — without needing to manually deal with QuickBMS commands or folder structures. Basically, to mod the game.
Technical Context of the Engine
The game uses a custom Korean visual novel engine (NekoNovel-style). Scripts are plain text files with Korean commands. Important commands include:

대사 → Normal dialogue
대사새줄 + 대사잇기 → Continue dialogue on new line
대기 → Wait for click
스크립트 이름.txt 주인공 / 이름지우기 → Show/hide character name
보이스 → Play voice
CG filename / 페이드인 / 페이드아웃 → Show images with fades
배경 / 배경룰페이드인 → Change background
효과음 / 배경음악 → Sound effects and BGM
딜레이 → Wait time
변수 → Variables
점프 / 북마크 → Jump / labels
쓰레드 / 쓰레드시작 → Threading for parallel actions
게임상태 → Game state
And many more (system menus, choices, achievements, etc.)

The archive format is .nkpack. We already have a working QuickBMS script (lucy.bms) that correctly extracts and reimports files when the folder structure is Scripts\filename.txt. This would be the essential core part of our editor/engine, cuz it's for packing and unpacking the game.
Required Features of the Application

Project System
Open game folder (asks for the original game path or files)
Automatically extract scripts into a clean working directory
Save project state

File Browser / Project Explorer
Tree view (or not) of all extracted scripts (chapters, character files, system files, etc.)
Easy search and filtering
Highlight modified files

Powerful Internal Text Editor
Syntax highlighting for Korean engine commands
Auto-completion for common commands
Fromat coding for dialogue, commands, names, jumps, etc.
Line numbers, folding, search & replace
Multiple tabs

One-Click Action Buttons / Command Palette (very important)
Create a rich toolbar or side panel with one-click buttons that insert properly formatted code blocks, for example:
Add normal dialogue
Add multi-line dialogue (대사새줄 + 대사잇기)
Add internal thought
Change background + fade
Show character CG + fade
Play sound effect
Play / stop BGM
Show / hide character name
Add delay
Create choice menu
Jump to label / create bookmark
Start/end thread
Fade out dialogue window
Scene transition
Set variable
Call another script
Achievement unlock block
etc.
Each button should insert clean, correctly indented, ready-to-use code with placeholders.
Sprite / Image Management
Ability to add new images/sprites
Preview of CGs and backgrounds
Easy insertion of image commands with correct naming

One-Click Actions
Extract Scripts
Pack / Reimport (must automatically create the correct reimport/Scripts/ structure and run QuickBMS with -w -r -r)
Run Game (launch Lucy.exe)
Open game folder
Restore original backup for specific scripts/packs

Quality of Life
English interface
Live preview of dialogue flow (optional but highly desired)
Error checking for common mistakes (missing 대기, broken jumps, etc.)
Auto-save

Technical Requirements
Windows first priority
Clean modern UI (Electron + modern GUI framework are all acceptable — choose the best balance of power and ease)
Must correctly handle the Scripts\ subfolder structure for reimport
Must call QuickBMS correctly under the hood (Read QUICKBMS_GUIDE.md)
Good error handling and user feedback


Deliverables
Please start by:

Proposing the best tech stack for this tool
Creating a detailed architecture and file structure
Designing the main UI layout
Implementing the core features step by step (starting with project loading + text editor + one-click packing)

Make the tool feel professional and enjoyable to use for community — something that turns the painful manual QuickBMS workflow and script/text editing into a smooth, creative experience.